This is a new crate, not a port of one repository. The code is new, with one exception: the ISO
21496-1 payload reader in src/iso.rs is a port of part of libultrahdr (below). The file layouts
come from the Ultra HDR format (Android, v1.1), CIPA DC-007 (Multi-Picture Format), the Adobe
HDR gain map XMP namespace and ISO/IEC 21496-1.

Third-party code
----------------

1. libultrahdr v2.0.2 (github.com/google/libultrahdr at e5f5a022fe96fc4dc2ee35c19f733a50df807abe),
   lib/src/gainmapmetadata.cpp. Copyright 2024 The Android Open Source Project. Licensed under
   the Apache License 2.0 or the MIT license, at your option.

   Ported: `decodeGainmapMetadata` (the big-endian field order, the flag bits, the common
   denominator form, copying channel 0 to the other channels) and
   `gainmapMetadataFractionToFloat` (non-zero denominators, `f32` division). The Rust code is in
   src/iso.rs (`IsoMetadata::parse`, `Metadata::from_iso`). The port is used here under the
   Apache License 2.0, which is the licence of this crate.

Tools used only in CI (no code copied, nothing linked into the crate)
---------------------------------------------------------------------

- libultrahdr v2.0.2 (Apache-2.0 or MIT), libjpeg-turbo 3.2.0 (BSD-3-Clause and IJG) and libavif
  v1.4.2 (BSD-2-Clause) are the parity oracles for the metadata and the pixels. They run as C or
  C++ tools built in CI.
- ExifTool 13.64 (GPL or Artistic licence) is the oracle for the XMP values. It is read as a
  behaviour reference only; no ExifTool code or tables are copied.

Dependencies
------------

github.com/dobbo-ca/jpeg-rs (JPEG decode), github.com/dobbo-ca/exif-rs (XMP parse) and
github.com/dobbo-ca/isobmff-rs (HEIF and AVIF boxes), all owner crates. See docs/dependencies.md.
